  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "Both aborts are fixed correctly: the `|| rc=$?` guard is scoped to the one `diff` call and keeps exit codes of 2 or more fatal, and `|| true` on the owner pipeline stops grep's no-match exit 1 from aborting under pipefail; the only weakness is that verification never ran two drifted files or showed the unassigned label being printed, and the agent admits this."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "The data, the workflow, the MISSING handling and the failure on drift are all untouched, but the agent added unrequested behavior changes: nullglob with a new hard error on an empty templates/ directory, `cut -f2-` in place of `-f2`, and `grep -m1` in place of `head -1`."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "The reply names the real failure mode: diff and grep exit 1 on expected results, and inside a command substitution under set -euo pipefail that aborts the script before the report prints; the verification account is muddled, though, since it says the scratch copy had an ownerless template and then says that case was not printed."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 7.6
  },
